-- title:
--   The pipeline error
-- statement:
--   **The pipeline error.** `F̃` is within `Es·hp` of the linear contraction `F` on grid inputs of norm `≤ 1/2`; `G = conj ∘ F ∘ conj`. For grid `u, v` of norm `≤ 1/4` and `Es·hp ≤ 1/100`, `z = Q_p(F̃u · F̃v)` is a grid array of norm `≤ 1/2` and `‖F̃⁺ z - G(Fu · Fv)‖ ≤ (3Es + 2)hp`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFMErr`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFM.pipeline_err (p : ℕ) {F Ft : (κ → ℂ) → (κ → ℂ)} (hF : LinC F) (Es : ℝ)
--       (hFt : ∀ u, Grid p u → ‖u‖ ≤ 1 / 2 → ‖Ft u - F u‖ ≤ Es * hp p)
--       (hEs : Es * hp p ≤ 1 / 100)
--       {u v : κ → ℂ} (hu : Grid p u) (hv : Grid p v) (hu1 : ‖u‖ ≤ 1 / 4) (hv1 : ‖v‖ ≤ 1 / 4) :
--       Grid p (QA p (Ft u * Ft v)) ∧ ‖QA p (Ft u * Ft v)‖ ≤ 1 / 2 ∧
--       ‖plusT Ft (QA p (Ft u * Ft v)) - cnj (F (cnj (F u * F v)))‖ ≤ (3 * Es + 2) * hp p
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFM 14: the error chain of the computed pipeline (§9.7.1), abstract form*: Arrays are functions `ι → ℂ` with the sup norm; `hp = 2^{-p}`. Every computed procedure is
--   an arbitrary function with an error bound on grid inputs (`Grid p f`: `Q_p f = f`), so the IL
--   denotations (and `P18IL`) plug in later.
